SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Mamas\, Apokrani monastery
LOCATION:Agios Mamas monastery (Apokrani)\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 1-2 September pilgrims head to the monastery of Agios Mamas\, perched on a cliff above the Libyan Sea south of the island: vespers\, then lamb offered by the shepherds\, roasted and served with pilaf\, dolmadakia and fried potatoes to 400-plus people by a chain of volunteers\, with the Perselis family playing the old Kasiot tunes. Many stay overnight in the monastery cells. The road is rough\; a 4x4 or a lift from a local helps.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#agios-mamas-monastery-apokrani-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-apokr
